  "result": "Issue #12 is implemented and the PR is open: https://github.com/acme/textstats/pull/7 (branch `feature/top-words-12`, commit `1f06f18`). The full test suite passes, 9 tests including 6 new ones for `top_words`.\n\n**Issue:** add `top_words(text, n)`. It returns up to `n` `(word, count)` tuples, most frequent first. Matching ignores case and punctuation, ties are broken alphabetically, and empty text returns `[]`. A reviewer asked for stdlib only.\n\n**What changed:**\n- **`textstats/__init__.py`:** added `top_words`. It lowercases the text, pulls out words with a regex that drops punctuation, counts them, sorts by highest count and then alphabetically, and returns the first `n`. It uses only `re` and `collections.Counter`.\n- **`tests/test_textstats.py`:** added tests for each acceptance criterion: order by frequency, the `n` limit, case, punctuation, tie-breaking and empty text.\n\nThe issue didn't cover two cases, so I chose how to handle them:\n- An apostrophe inside a word is kept, so `don't` counts as one word rather than `don` and `t`.\n- If `n` is 0 or negative, the function returns `[]`.\n\nThe commit message says `Closes #12`, so the issue will close when the PR is merged.",
